================================================================================
SECTION 2: DIVERGENCE ABORT IMPLEMENTATION
================================================================================

2.1 DivergenceAbort() Function Signature
-----------------------------------------
Location: src/engine/ingress/DivergenceAbort.h
          src/engine/ingress/DivergenceAbort.cpp

Function signature:
  [[noreturn]] void DivergenceAbort(const AbortContext& context) noexcept;

Behavior:
  1. Log error to stderr (atomic write, unbuffered)
  2. Flush all caches (stdout, stderr, streams)
  3. Emergency shutdown (best-effort cleanup)
  4. Exit with code 42 (using std::_Exit() - no destructors)

Exit code: 42 (chosen to distinguish from standard exit codes)
           - Standard exit(0) = success
           - Standard exit(1) = generic error
           - DIVERGENCE_ABORT = 42 = data integrity failure

2.2 AbortContext Structure
---------------------------
struct AbortContext {
  AbortCategory category;        // Error category (see below)
  const char* file;              // Source file (__FILE__)
  int line;                      // Source line (__LINE__)
  const char* function;          // Function name (__func__)
  std::string_view message;      // Human-readable error message

  // Optional diagnostics
  uint64_t expected_hash;        // For hash mismatches
  uint64_t actual_hash;          // For hash mismatches
  size_t resource_requested;     // For OOM
  size_t resource_available;     // For OOM
};

2.3 Emergency Shutdown Logic
-----------------------------
Emergency shutdown sequence (DivergenceAbort.cpp):
  1. flushCaches() - flush stdout/stderr streams
  2. Best-effort cleanup (no memory release - may be corrupt)
  3. std::_Exit(42) - immediate termination without destructors

Rationale for std::_Exit() vs std::exit():
  - std::exit() runs destructors - may fail if memory is corrupt
  - std::_Exit() terminates immediately - safe for corrupted state
  - POSIX _Exit() guarantees no signal handlers or atexit() calls

2.4 Logging Format
------------------
Abort log format (stderr):
  ============================================================
  DIVERGENCE ABORT - FAIL-CLOSED SHUTDOWN
  ============================================================
  Timestamp:  YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS.mmm
  Category:   <ABORT_CATEGORY>
  Location:   <file>:<line>
  Function:   <function>
  Message:    <error message>
  [Category-specific diagnostics]
  ============================================================
  System integrity compromised. Aborting to prevent partial results.
  Exit code: 42 (DIVERGENCE_ABORT)
  ============================================================

