SECTION 3: ERROR CATEGORIES MAPPED TO ABORT BEHAVIOR
================================================================================

3.1 Abort Category Definitions
-------------------------------
enum class AbortCategory : uint8_t {
  // CRITICAL: Data integrity violations (MUST abort)
  HASH_MISMATCH          = 1,   // Digest verification failed
  CORRUPT_INDEX_DATA     = 2,   // Index data corruption detected
  EPOCH_VIOLATION        = 3,   // Epoch guard breach

  // CRITICAL: Resource exhaustion (MUST abort)
  OUT_OF_MEMORY          = 10,  // Memory allocation failed
  RESOURCE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED = 11, // Resource guard breach

  // CRITICAL: Missing critical files (MUST abort)
  MISSING_CRITICAL_FILE  = 20,  // Required file not found
  IO_CORRUPTION          = 21,  // I/O error indicating corruption

  // CRITICAL: Guard breaches (MUST abort)
  GUARD_BREACH           = 30,  // Any guard violation
  INVARIANT_VIOLATION    = 31,  // Structural invariant violated

  // INTERNAL: Unexpected states (MUST abort)
  INTERNAL_ERROR         = 100, // Unexpected internal error
};

3.2 Error Category Mapping (IngressErrorCode → AbortCategory)
--------------------------------------------------------------

ABORT-WORTHY ERRORS (trigger DivergenceAbort):
  IngressErrorCode                 → AbortCategory
  ----------------------------------------------------------------
  BUFFER_OVERFLOW                  → GUARD_BREACH
  MEMORY_ALLOCATION_FAILED         → OUT_OF_MEMORY
  RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED               → RESOURCE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED
  DIGEST_MISMATCH                  → HASH_MISMATCH
  NORMALIZATION_FAILED (critical)  → CORRUPT_INDEX_DATA
  FILE_NOT_FOUND (critical files)  → MISSING_CRITICAL_FILE
  IO_ERROR (corruption detected)   → IO_CORRUPTION
  INTERNAL_ERROR                   → INTERNAL_ERROR

NON-ABORT ERRORS (return error code, do not execute):
  IngressErrorCode                 → Behavior
  ----------------------------------------------------------------
  UNSUPPORTED_FORMAT               → Return error (user input issue)
  JSONLD_MISSING_CONTEXT           → Return error (validation failure)
  VALIDATION_SHAPE_VIOLATION       → Return error (input validation)
  PARSE_ERROR_SYNTAX               → Return error (malformed input)
  [All validation errors]          → Return error code

Rationale:
  - User input errors (malformed JSON, wrong format) → return error code
  - System integrity errors (OOM, corruption, guards) → ABORT IMMEDIATELY

3.3 Convenience Macros
----------------------
#define DIVERGENCE_ABORT(category, message)
  → Aborts with source location (__FILE__, __LINE__, __func__)

#define DIVERGENCE_ABORT_HASH_MISMATCH(expected, actual, message)
  → Aborts with hash diagnostic info

#define DIVERGENCE_ABORT_OOM(requested, available, message)
  → Aborts with memory allocation diagnostic info

#define DIVERGENCE_ABORT_GUARD_BREACH(message)
  → Aborts for guard violations

#define DIVERGENCE_ABORT_EPOCH_VIOLATION(message)
  → Aborts for epoch violations

#define DIVERGENCE_CHECK(condition, category, message)
  → Abort if condition is false

#define DIVERGENCE_CHECK_HASH(expected, actual, message)
  → Abort if hashes don't match

